```

# FILES

: `/proc/<pid>/status`
  Each process's status record.

# SEE ALSO

procfs(4), kill(1), ns(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

`ps` says `ps: cannot read /proc` and exits `no /proc` when `/proc` cannot be opened, and exits `no namespace` when it was given none.

# BUGS

`id=` repeats `pid`.

There are no columns, no times and no user: the line is the status record as procfs writes it.
